in the world of cars there are Ferraris  and then there are Ferrari the $320,000  Ferrari f12berlinetta  is decidedly the latter we are in the  Mojave Desert in the middle of a wind  farm and it's the perfect juxtaposition  to this 12 cylinder gas guzzling f12  Berlinetta it gets an astounding 731  horsepower and it'll hit 62 miles per  hour at 3.1 seconds  everything in this car is oriented  toward making me want to go faster  this is the car that Ferrari made to  drive to the track drive on the track  and then drive home from the track  I'm also really happy to report that the  interior is big there's lots of head and  leg room there's plenty of shoulder room  these are racing style sports seats that  are adjustable in a dozen ways you're  gonna be fine with them there are a few  blind spots behind your rear left and  right corners and don't expect to take  this car over any dips higher than speed  oh and expect to get no more than 18  miles per gallon tops but those are  small prices to pay for near perfection  in the driving machine Ferrari is  extremely proud of what it has achieved  with this modern Berlinetta and  rightfully so it's the most powerful  Ferrari Road car ever built I loved it  to my mind the Ferrari California is the  car you buy your spouse or your son the  f12 berlinetta this is the one you'll  want to keep for yourself
 

